-- title:
--   Weight-two Γ(N)-invariance of (a/b) (c/e)'
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$, and let $A_N \subseteq (\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C})$ be the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), defined as the $\mathbb{C}$-algebra generated by the function `jAnalytic` together with all the functions `fricke N v` for $v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$ with $v \neq 0$. Let $F : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be holomorphic, in the sense of being differentiable for the standard complex-manifold structures on the upper half-plane and on $\mathbb{C}$, and let $a, b, c, e : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be four elements of $A_N$ with $b$ and $e$ not the zero function. Assume that for every $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$ one has $$F(\tau)\, b(\tau)\, e(\tau)^2 = a(\tau)\bigl(e(\tau)\, c'(\tau) - c(\tau)\, e'(\tau)\bigr),$$ where the derivatives are the complex derivatives at $\tau$ of the compositions of $c$ and $e$ with `UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`; informally, $F = (a/b)\,(c/e)'$ away from the zeros of $be$. Then for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(N)$, the weight-$2$ slash action leaves $F$ unchanged: $F \mid_2 \gamma = F$ as functions on $\mathbb{H}$.
--
--   This is the automorphy half of the classical description of differentials of the first kind on the modular curve $X(N)$: a function of the form $(a/b)\,d(c/e)/d\tau$ with $a,b,c,e$ modular functions of level $N$ transforms with weight $2$ under $\Gamma(N)$. It is used in the construction of an injective linear map from regular differentials to cusp forms, [`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective).
